       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use.\n- **Single dose:** The maximum for one dose is usually 800 mg, so 1600 mg exceeds that as well.\n- **Risk:** At this dose the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events is much higher.\n\nPossible intended orders include:\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1600 mg total per day, split into smaller doses\n\nPlease tell me which dose and frequency you want, or confirm that 1600 mg four times daily is intended. If you confirm it, I'd want to know the clinical rationale first. I can then enter the corrected order right away."
