       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily dose. Each 1600 mg dose is also double the maximum single dose. I can't think of an indication that justifies it, and it carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you need more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than these give, I'd suggest discussing options with pharmacy. These could include adding acetaminophen or choosing a different agent. If there is a protocol or specialist recommendation behind this dose, pharmacy can review it and help get it ordered through the right channel.\n\nWhich of these would you like me to enter?"
